// `volatile` is not a Kama keyword — the MMIO/ISR qualifier is spelled `hardware` (emits C `volatile`).
// `static volatile int32 reg` is a plain syntax error (the accepted forms are in
// tests/hardware_static_{flag,ptr}.kama). This guards that `volatile` is never silently accepted.
static volatile int32 reg = 0;
fn int32 main() { return 0; }
